<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- The user picks ~/.claude in an open panel; we keep it across launches
	     as an app-scoped bookmark. Both halves are required: the panel grant
	     without the bookmark dies at the next launch. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
	<true/>

	<!--
	No network entitlements at all, in either direction, and both absences are
	deliberate.

	com.apple.security.network.server was here until 2026-08-16, for the
	loopback listener the Claude Code hook bridge uses. App Review asked about
	it twice under guideline 2.4.5, and they were right: the bridge cannot work
	in this build. HookInstaller edits ~/.claude/settings.json, and inside the
	sandbox the home directory is the container, so enabling it would have
	written a hook file somewhere Claude Code never looks. The listener is off
	in this build (PreciseDetection.isSupported), the control that offered it is
	hidden, and verify-mas-build.sh fails if either the entitlement or a
	listener symbol comes back. Detection here is the transcript watcher, which
	needs no network.

	com.apple.security.network.client has never been here. Belay has nothing to
	phone home to. Anything that would need it, Sparkle, analytics, a crash
	reporter, does not ship in this channel. Adding it is a product decision,
	not a build fix.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
